* sg13g2-lc-pll :: sim/divider-elab -- ELABORATION of the divider netlist for five N codes (issue #32).
* One ngspice process, one short transient (30 ns, 100 MHz clock; the registered-flag counters of issue #61 have no usable
* DC .op: the tied-input operating point of the latch-rich netlist does not converge). This proves only that
* design/netlist/divider.spice parses, resolves every subcircuit and model, and runs with each code tied; it grades no behaviour. Nominal corner
* (hbt_typ, mos_tt, cap_typ), 27 C, 3.3 V. Placeholders (@@...@@) are filled by scripts/run-divider-elab.sh.
* N = 8 M + 2 A (prescaler P = 8/10, issue #43): 100 = (12,2); 90 = (11,1); 110 = (13,3); A = 0 and A = 3 at M = 12.
.lib @@MODELS_DIR@@/cornerHBT.lib hbt_typ
.lib @@MODELS_DIR@@/cornerMOShv.lib mos_tt
.lib @@MODELS_DIR@@/cornerCAP.lib cap_typ
.lib @@MODELS_DIR@@/cornerRES.lib res_typ
.option temp=27
.include @@DIV_NETLIST@@

VDD vdd 0 3.3
V1 one 0 dc 3.3
IRF vdd iref dc 50u
XQR iref iref rr 0 npn13G2v Nx=1 El=1
RR rr 0 2400
VIP inp 0 dc 3.18 sin(3.18 0.2 100meg)
VIN inn 0 dc 3.18 sin(3.18 -0.2 100meg)
* M3 M2 M1 M0   A2 A1 A0 (pin order is M0 M1 M2 M3 A0 A1 A2)
Xn100 inp inn iref 0 0 one one 0 0 one mc100 fb100 vdd 0 divider
Xn90  inp inn iref one one 0 one 0 one 0 mc90 fb90 vdd 0 divider
Xn110 inp inn iref one 0 one one 0 one one mc110 fb110 vdd 0 divider
Xa0   inp inn iref 0 0 one one 0 0 0 mca0 fba0 vdd 0 divider
Xa7   inp inn iref 0 0 one one one one one mca7 fba7 vdd 0 divider
.save v(mc100) v(mc90) v(mc110) v(mca0) v(mca7)

.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_PSP@@
pre_osdi @@OSDI_PSP_NQS@@
pre_osdi @@OSDI_R3@@
tran 100p 30n 0 100p
echo "ELAB_OK n100 n90 n110 a0 a7"
.endc
.end
